    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d645">

                <pb facs="0698" n="590" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg590"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.0084/39</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Vice Consul at Aden</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Park</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-02-07"><hi rendition="#italic">February 7,
                        1927</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department duly received Mr. Totten’s
                    despatch No. 5 of June 17 last,<anchor n="6" xml:id="d645-f1"/> transmitting a
                    sealed envelope containing two letters addressed to the President by His
                    Imperial Highness, Ras Taffari Makonnen, Prince Regent of the Empire and Heir to
                    the Throne of Ethiopia. One of these letters concerned two elephant tusks which
                    the Prince sent as a personal gift to the President,<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d645-f2"/> and the other related to the establishment of a
                    diplomatic mission at Addis Ababa.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d645-f3"/></p>
                <p>The Department now encloses the President’s replies to the communications from
                    the Prince, together with office copies thereof, as well as copies for the files
                    of the Consulate.</p>
                <p>The office copies should be transmitted to the appropriate office of the
                    Ethiopian Government and the original letters transmitted to their destination
                    in the manner that may be most agreeable to His Imperial Highness.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J.
                            Butler Wright</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d645-a1.xml" xpointer="d645-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
